(6603215, 985104, 124190, '<td valign="top">PHEWWWWWWW......have not really looked quite this closely before.....reaffirms my crazy notions of the tiny being infinitesimally  cosmic.....(sounds trippy I know ) BUT I went to the Smithsonian Air and Space Museum once when I was much younger and they had a video display of the most current satellite pictures from outermost space.....the theme of the video was a zoom into earth from that outermost photograph/video they had and it went closer and closer to earth and then in as close as possible with photos of minute details from an electron microscope.....am I explaining this so you understand?   ANYWAY...your shot looks like a BLACK HOLE!!!!! The beginning of "time" cosmic blast...whatever.....   why does everything small look like something from outer space.........    awesome!</td>', 'PHEWWWWWWW......have not really looked quite this closely before.....reaffirms my crazy notions of the tiny being infinitesimally  cosmic.....(sounds trippy I know ) BUT I went to the Smithsonian Air and Space Museum once when I was much younger and they had a video display of the most current satellite pictures from outermost space.....the theme of the video was a zoom into earth from that outermost photograph/video they had and it went closer and closer to earth and then in as close as possible with photos of minute details from an electron microscope.....am I explaining this so you understand?   ANYWAY...your shot looks like a BLACK HOLE!!!!! The beginning of "time" cosmic blast...whatever.....   why does everything small look like something from outer space.........    awesome!', '2011-11-25 09:57:37.000000', NULL, 1),
