(6611710, 985168, 62357, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club Don.<br/> <br/>It''s been a while since I''ve done a critique club comment, so bear with me, I''m a bit rusty.  I also always find it challenging to do an in depth critique of your images for some reason I can''t quite put my finger on.<br/> <br/>I suppose it was no surprise to you to get a lowish vote, as it''s totally an out of the box image when thinking of the challenge topic.  I see where you are coming from now when lingering over it,  but probably, had I voted in the challenge, would have also scratched my head a bit wondering how it fitted.  <br/> <br/>However, as a standalone image I rather like it.  I like the composition and don''t find anything to complain about concerning the black and white conversion.  It made me think, which is a good thing.  Therefore, in conclusion despite the low score, I still think it''s a good ''un.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club Don. It''s been a while since I''ve done a critique club comment, so bear with me, I''m a bit rusty.  I also always find it challenging to do an in depth critique of your images for some reason I can''t quite put my finger on. I suppose it was no surprise to you to get a lowish vote, as it''s totally an out of the box image when thinking of the challenge topic.  I see where you are coming from now when lingering over it,  but probably, had I voted in the challenge, would have also scratched my head a bit wondering how it fitted.   However, as a standalone image I rather like it.  I like the composition and don''t find anything to complain about concerning the black and white conversion.  It made me think, which is a good thing.  Therefore, in conclusion despite the low score, I still think it''s a good ''un.', '2011-12-06 07:22:43.000000', NULL, 0),
